      "form_guide": "",
      "comment": "SONNIG (5) is the top pick, with the strength of her Hawkesbury CL1 win two starts back still the key reference. She beat Blue Eyed Brigid there at big odds, who has since won and performed admirably in town, and while the Kembla effort last start was plain, she gets a more suitable setup this time around. AUTUMN SKY (4) ran fourth at Newcastle in a CL1 and now easing back from provincial company third-up, with Alysha Collett a positive booking. Looks set to play a role. ANGEL IN THE WIND (3) arrives off a Nowra BM58 win where she was wide throughout and still got there. The way she finished off suggests this distance isn't an issue now and it wouldn't surprise to see her repeat the dose. KURITHEA (6) gets the blinkers on today back in trip and she can run an improved race. SNAP DECISION (2) is coming back in trip which is a query, though he's right on the cusp of another win.",
